From: kaiter <kaiter@example.com>
Date: Thu, 14 Nov 2026 03:11:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pcie: Skip PCIe training in U-Boot for sun60iw2

This patch prevents U-Boot from performing PCIe link training, which causes
the system to hang when PCIe2 is misidentified as PCIe3 during enumeration.

Known Issue:
- U-Boot PCIe training on A7Z hangs the boot process
- PCIe2 controller is mistakenly identified as PCIe3
- The timeout during training causes indefinite hang
- Linux kernel can properly detect PCIe once U-Boot skips training

Solution:
- Check for skip-uboot-pcie-training device tree property
- Skip PCIe controller initialization in U-Boot
- Allow Linux kernel to handle PCIe detection and training

This allows successful boot with or without PCIe devices attached.

Signed-off-by: kaiter <kaiter@example.com>
---
 drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c b/drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
@@ -1,6 +1,31 @@
+#include <common.h>
+#include <dm.h>
+#include <fdtdec.h>
+
+static int sunxi_pcie_skip_training(struct udevice *dev)
+{
+	ofnode node;
+	int skip = 0;
+
+	node = dev_get_ofnode(dev);
+	if (ofnode_valid(node)) {
+		skip = ofnode_read_bool(node, "skip-uboot-pcie-training");
+	}
+
+	return skip;
+}
+
+static int sunxi_pcie_probe(struct udevice *dev)
+{
+	/* Skip PCIe training if device tree indicates it */
+	if (sunxi_pcie_skip_training(dev)) {
+		printf("PCIe: Skipping U-Boot training (will be handled by kernel)\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	/* Original PCIe probe code continues here */
+	return sunxi_pcie_probe_original(dev);
+}
 
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Allwinner PCIe platform driver");
